Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> expression
Rule 1     expression -> expression PLUS term
Rule 2     expression -> expression MINUS term
Rule 3     expression -> term
Rule 4     term -> factor
Rule 5     term -> term TIMES factor
Rule 6     term -> term DIVIDE factor
Rule 7     factor -> NUMBER
Rule 8     factor -> VARIABLE
Rule 9     factor -> PAREN_OPEN expression PAREN_CLOSE
Rule 10    factor -> MINUS factor
Rule 11    factor -> FUNCTION PAREN_OPEN expression PAREN_CLOSE

Terminals, with rules where they appear

DIVIDE               : 6
FUNCTION             : 11
MINUS                : 2 10
NUMBER               : 7
PAREN_CLOSE          : 9 11
PAREN_OPEN           : 9 11
PLUS                 : 1
TIMES                : 5
VARIABLE             : 8
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

expression           : 1 2 9 11 0
factor               : 4 5 6 10
term                 : 1 2 3 5 6

Parsing method: LALR

